  "usage_note": "**Even** alone cannot join two clauses. To give a fact that does not change what follows, use **even though** (*Even though it was raining, we went out*); for a possible situation, use **even if** (*I'll go even if it rains*).",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "Even he is rich, he is not happy.",
      "correct": "Even though he is rich, he is not happy.",
      "note": "Use **even though** or **even if** to begin a clause; **even** alone cannot join two clauses."
    }
